## Description
A client object's remote method may declare return type `never`, and nutcracker accepts it. Spec §5.6.3.4 Remote methods (https://ballerina.io/spec/lang/master/#section_5.6.3.4): "A remote method of a client object can only be invoked by a client-remote-method-call-action. The return type of the remote method of a client object must not be never." Neither the spec deviations nor the subset restrictions in subset10.md mention this case. Client classes (`remote-method-defn`) and `remote-method-decl` in object type descriptors are both listed as supported.

## Steps to Reproduce
Client class:
```ballerina
client class Cl {
    remote function r() returns never { // @error
        panic error("x");
    }
}

public function main() {
}
```
Client object type descriptor:
```ballerina
type CT client object {
    remote function r() returns never; // @error
};

public function main() {
}
```
Actual: both compile and run, exiting with code 0.
Expected: a compile error on each remote method declaration.

## Affected Version(s)
upstream main @ 1bcb85b9

## OS, DB, other environment details and versions
Linux, `go run ./cli/cmd run <file.bal>`

## Related area
Semantics

## Suggested label(s) (optional)
